adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the secret check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET)
  return 403;
```

If `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is `undefined` (env var not set at all) and the request also omits that header, then `req.headers[...]` is `undefined`, making the comparison `undefined !== undefined` evaluate to `false`, so the request is accepted (assuming `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` is true). This is a real authentication bypass introduced by the current logic. The constant-time-compare point is secondary, but the unset-secret bypass is directly verifiable from the diff.
